RETIRED 2026-08-26 by agent session, per user instruction.

This patch attempted to fix a suspected "WiFi/SDIO left in stuck state after a
plain warm reboot" issue by forcing RK3308 boards to use watchdog-triggered
reset instead of normal soft reset whenever no explicit reboot mode command is
given.

Live-tested on 2026-08-26 (genuine factory firmware, board reachable via SSH
at your-host): a plain `sudo reboot` (normal soft reset, no watchdog forcing)
fully restored WiFi within seconds (wpa_state=COMPLETED, real tx/rx traffic).
The earlier "needs special reset handling" symptom was traced to stuck chip
state from manual rmmod/modprobe/rfkill/GPIO-toggle testing during a live
diagnostic session, NOT a real requirement for normal boot-to-boot operation.

This patch is very likely unnecessary. Retired rather than deleted in case
future testing on OUR OWN kernel/build (mainline 6.18 + out-of-tree rtl8189fs,
different from factory's vendor 5.10 kernel) reveals a genuine need for it --
if so, re-apply and validate specifically on our build with a clean-boot test
methodology (no manual driver manipulation before checking WiFi state).
